      "Chapter 3 — Save your first money and build stability\nEarning money is only half of Level 1. The other half is keeping enough of it to create choices.",
      "Build a basic cash buffer\nStart with a realistic target:\n- First target: cover an immediate unexpected expense.\n- Next target: one month of essential expenses.\n- Later target: several months of essential expenses, adjusted to income stability and responsibilities.\nThe source uses $1,000–$10,000 as a broad savings target. Your personal emergency fund may need to be lower or higher depending on local costs and obligations.",
