      "Chapter 7 — Route 3: Build an agency from a service\nThe source describes an agency as taking a skill or service and delivering it at a larger scale for businesses or individuals. It suggests that freelancing can be a logical first step: learn the skill, get clients, understand delivery, then train or hire others to help fulfil the work.",
      "Why freelancing can come first\nFreelancing teaches you:\n- What clients actually buy.\n- What a good deliverable looks like.\n- How long the work takes.\n- Which requests are profitable.\n- What clients complain about.\n- Which parts can be standardised.\n- How to price and scope projects.\nWithout this knowledge, hiring a team can multiply mistakes.",
