      "Chapter 13 — Opportunity 5: Speculative investments, including crypto\nThe source suggests that someone at this stage may allocate some capital to crypto because they can avoid risking their entire life savings. It refers to a future bull run and the possibility of large gains.",
      "That is the source's opinion, not a dependable investment strategy. A future bull market is uncertain, and crypto assets can lose substantial value. Some projects fail entirely; custody, exchange, fraud, volatility, and regulatory risks also matter.",
      "A safer decision framework\nBefore buying any speculative asset, ask:\n- What exactly am I buying?\n- What creates its value?\n- What could cause it to fall sharply?\n- Can I lose the full amount?\n- How much of my total portfolio would it represent?\n- What is my time horizon?\n- What is my exit or rebalancing rule?\n- Am I relying on hype, leverage, or a prediction?\nDo not use emergency savings or borrowed money for speculative investments. Diversification and position sizing can reduce concentration risk but cannot eliminate losses.",
      "The Level 3 capital-allocation worksheet\nFor each opportunity, record:\n| Question | Your answer |\n| --- | --- |\n| What is the asset or business? |  |\n| Why do I believe it can produce value? |  |\n| What evidence supports the thesis? |  |\n| How much capital is required? |  |\n| What additional cash may be needed? |  |\n| What is the realistic downside? |  |\n| How liquid is the investment? |  |\n| What could make the thesis wrong? |  |\n| What is the time horizon? |  |\n| How will I monitor it? |  |\n| What is my exit or stop decision? |  |",
      "Level 3 exit checklist\n- [ ] You have a meaningful savings and investment base.\n- [ ] You understand the difference between income, profit, cash flow, and net worth.\n- [ ] Your capital is not concentrated in one untested opportunity.\n- [ ] You have begun acquiring or building assets with a clear rationale.\n- [ ] Your business can operate with less dependence on your daily labour.\n- [ ] You understand the risks and obligations of each investment.\n- [ ] Your lifestyle has not expanded so quickly that it consumes all progress.\nPart 5 — Level 4: Alpha Chad"
