    "id": "chapter-23",
    "number": 23,
    "title": "Chapter 23 — Keep Risk Proportional to Your Position",
    "paragraphs": [
      "Chapter 23 — Keep risk proportional to your position\nThe source's progression implies that a person with more capital can take on larger opportunities. That does not mean risk should grow unchecked.",
      "A sensible approach is to ask:\n- Can I afford the downside?\n- Is the investment diversified?\n- Is the expected return worth the risk?\n- Is the opportunity understandable?\n- Can I exit if circumstances change?\n- Am I using leverage?\n- What happens if income stops?\n- Have I obtained independent advice where needed?\nThe more capital and responsibility you have, the more important risk management becomes."
    ]
